# Sizing for the local overlay, in one place. up.sh and the tests read this file;
# kustomization.yaml carries the matching per-pod requests and limits, and
# tests/deploy/local-sizing.test.ts fails when the two disagree.
#
# PROVISIONAL: the floor below is a starting point, to be measured. It is
# "whatever passes verify-turns.sh twice in a row without a 'could not measure'
# on that host", and that run has not been done on a host this small yet. The
# only measurement so far: a 3 CPU / 3.5 GB minikube node inside a 4 CPU / 6 GB
# Docker VM, which had roughly 100 MB free under verification load.

# Default size of the minikube node (overridable: SLAUDE_LOCAL_CPUS, SLAUDE_LOCAL_MEMORY).
LOCAL_NODE_CPUS=3
LOCAL_NODE_MEMORY_MB=3500

# Provisional minimum Docker VM that hosts that node. up.sh warns below it.
LOCAL_VM_FLOOR_CPUS=4
LOCAL_VM_FLOOR_MEMORY_MB=6144

# What the node keeps for itself (kubelet, apiserver, coredns, metrics-server).
# The summed pod LIMITS at the pinned replica counts (2 gateways, 2 nodes, one
# Postgres, one Redis) must fit the node size minus these.
LOCAL_SYSTEM_RESERVE_MILLICPU=200
LOCAL_SYSTEM_RESERVE_MEMORY_MB=500

# Per-node-pod headroom. A node pod holds the bun process plus one `claude` CLI
# child per warm session, measured at roughly 150-200 MB each (the 2026-10-01
# remote-exec field note). The node limit must cover bun plus three warm
# sessions: 200 + 3 x 200 = 800 MB, so the 896 Mi limit leaves a little over.
LOCAL_NODE_BASE_MB=200
LOCAL_NODE_SESSION_MB=200
LOCAL_NODE_WARM_SESSIONS=3

# Limits arithmetic at the pinned counts (2 gateways, 2 nodes, Postgres, Redis):
#   gateway 2 x 448 + node 2 x 896 + postgres 240 + redis 64 = 2992 MB
#   available: 3500 - 500 reserve = 3000 MB.
# The documented flow also deploys Keycloak (panel.sh: request 512 Mi, limit
# 1 Gi) and mock-mcp (request 64 Mi, limit 256 Mi). They are NOT in the limits
# sum, which would reach ~4250 MB: limits are overcommitted by design for those
# optional add-ons, and it is their REQUESTS that must fit (2496 MB with every
# add-on at the HPA maximum of three nodes). local-sizing.test.ts checks both.
